From ab330a597316e323d8f3572d263e8b9e99b8dec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dingo <outbackdingo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:18:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] kernels: move cuda-oxide pins to NVIDIA/cuda-rust tip
 d141118c (was b9847e9, 301 commits behind)

Migrate off cuda-oxide rev b9847e9 to the current tip of NVlabs/cuda-oxide
(now redirecting to NVIDIA/cuda-rust), rev
d141118c05f705fcf932a8e9077dc714477edc4d:

  * 80 cuda-device/cuda-host pins bumped b9847e9 -> d141118c (40 manifests)
  * 41 "cuda-core = 0.3.1" (crates.io) requirements replaced with the git
    dep at the same tip rev. kdiff is a second consumer, so a 0.3.1
    crates.io requirement plus a git 0.4.0 both land in the graph and
    cuda_core::simt::context::CudaContext stops unifying. Moving the
    requirement itself (not [patch.crates-io]) yields exactly one
    cuda-core 0.4.0.

Requires nightly-2026-10-11: the tip's cuda-host uses the reflection
intrinsic and fails on nightly-2026-08-28 with
error[E0433]: cannot find `reflection` in `intrinsics`.

Buys the sparse-FP8 metadata fix (#1483 preserves rustc reference
attributes) and toolchain alignment. Kernel sources untouched; the
measured API drift is zero once the version skew is fixed.

Verified: all 39 crate modules codegen at sm_120; engine rebuilt and
generates; littlebit gate 9/9 worst rel 5.878e-7 (unchanged).
